                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Carll, United
                        States marshal, to Mr. Field, Assistant
                        Attorney-General</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">New Haven,
                        Connecticut</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1869-07-02"
                            ><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 2, 1869</date>.</dateline>
                <p rendition="#flush">Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. A. Field</hi>,<lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">Assistant United States Attorney-General:</hi></p>
                <p>The schooners Fancy and Winona both at the dock in New Haven, with a portion of
                    cargo; balance of cargo in Milford; all in my custody, awaiting further
                    orders.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>P. R. CARLL,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">United States
                        Marshal.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
